        "side": "new",
        "severity": "high",
        "category": "bug",
        "title": "Returning related FK field makes changelist display wrong object or crash",
        "explanation": "lookup_field now returns the final field of any `__` path, not only boolean ones. In admin_list.items_for_result, when f is not None and f.remote_field is a ManyToOneRel (FK/OneToOne as the final hop), the value is recomputed as `getattr(result, f.name)` on the *root* object, ignoring the traversed `value`. For list_display = ['parent__parent'] on GrandChild this shows GrandChild.parent (the Child) instead of Child.parent (the Parent). If the root model has no attribute named f.name (e.g. 'group__owner' where only Group has 'owner'), it raises AttributeError and the changelist page crashes. Before this change f was None, so the traversed value was shown correctly via display_for_value.",
        "suggestion": "Only set f when the final field is not a relation, e.g. `field = get_fields_from_path(opts.model, name)[-1]; if not field.is_relation: f = field`. Alternatively, change items_for_result to use the already-resolved `value` for related fields. Add a test with a list_display path that ends in a FK.",
        "evidence": "                        f = get_fields_from_path(opts.model, name)[-1]",
        "confidence": 0.72,
        "id": "95b6719324e3",
